@* Help — the boundary, stated plainly, and the route out.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Reachable from the nav, and directly from every refusal, failed gate check
   and no-cache error state in the app: the person who most needs the boundary
   spelled out is the one who just hit it, not the one browsing a menu.

   Entirely static, and that is a requirement rather than a convenience. The
   offline path through this app terminates here, so this page has to be
   readable with no signal at all. Nothing on it fetches anything, and that
   includes the disclosure below — <details> is browser behaviour, so a section
   opens with no JavaScript, no state, and nothing to load.

   EIGHT SECTIONS AT ONE LEVEL, ALL CLOSED. It used to be four long blocks read
   top to bottom regardless of which one you came for. The five lifecycle stages
   are now peers of the other three categories rather than nested inside one of
   them, which is what makes the page read as a list of answerable questions
   instead of a single document. Somebody arriving from a specific refusal
   should not have to scroll past four sections they did not come for.

   NO URL-FRAGMENT AUTO-EXPAND. Opening the relevant section from a link is the
   obvious next step and it is deliberately not built: 09 §7.3 names it as an
   extension and explicitly does not authorize it. Raised in the Completion
   Report rather than assumed here.

   The content inventory is unchanged. The same four categories, the same five
   stages, the same words — translated, and disclosed rather than stacked. The
   contact section in particular still says what it said: it is not an appeal
   channel, and collapsing it changed its visibility, not its framing. *@

@page "/help"
@inject LocaleService L

<PageTitle>@L[Locale, "help.title"]</PageTitle>

<h1>@L[Locale, "help.title"]</h1>

<p class="help__intro">@L[Locale, "help.intro"]</p>

<p class="help__hint">@L[Locale, "help.hint"]</p>

@* --- Staged guidance, flattened into its five stages ------------------- *@

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.beforeApply.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.beforeApply.body"]</p>
</details>

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.beingAssessed.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.beingAssessed.body"]</p>
</details>

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.decision.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@((MarkupString)L[Locale, "help.decision.body"])</p>
</details>

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.tournament.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.tournament.body"]</p>
</details>

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.matchday.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.matchday.body"]</p>
</details>

@* --- What this service does not do ------------------------------------- *@

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.notDo.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.notDo.visasStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.notDo.visasBody"]</li>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.notDo.vettingStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.notDo.vettingBody"]</li>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.notDo.quotaStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.notDo.quotaBody"]</li>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.notDo.guaranteeStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.notDo.guaranteeBody"]</li>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.notDo.appealsStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.notDo.appealsBody"]</li>
    </ul>
</details>

@* --- What will not notify you ------------------------------------------ *@

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.notNotify.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.notNotify.intro"]</p>
    <ul>
        <li>@L[Locale, "help.notNotify.item1"]</li>
        <li>@L[Locale, "help.notNotify.item2"]</li>
        <li>@((MarkupString)L[Locale, "help.notNotify.item3"])</li>
        <li>@L[Locale, "help.notNotify.item4"]</li>
    </ul>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.notNotify.closing"]</p>
</details>

@* --- The escalation route, which is not an appeal channel -------------- *@

<details class="help__section">
    <summary class="help__summary"><h2>@L[Locale, "help.contact.heading"]</h2></summary>
    <p>@L[Locale, "help.contact.intro"]</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.contact.officerStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.contact.officerBody"]</li>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.contact.centreStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.contact.centreBody"]</li>
        <li><strong>@L[Locale, "help.contact.fifaStrong"]</strong> @L[Locale, "help.contact.fifaBody"]</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="help__mocked">@L[Locale, "help.contact.mocked"]</p>
</details>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public AppLocale Locale { get; set; }
}
